WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.082
The villagers gathered around Gau.

2
00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:05.318
He groaned in pain.

3
00:00:05.319 --> 00:00:10.177
Suddenly some women appeared, howling and screaming.

4
00:00:10.178 --> 00:00:14.480
The villagers began to clap loudly and chant.

5
00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:20.140
A man wearing bracelets on his wrists and ankles jumped into the fire.

6
00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:23.080
"Wow!" said Vinnie.

7
00:00:23.081 --> 00:00:27.883
The man began dancing and jumped in and out of the fire.

8
00:00:27.884 --> 00:00:33.179
He waved his arms above his head and then moved over to Gau.

9
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:37.553
The healer placed his hands on Gau’s leg.

10
00:00:37.554 --> 00:00:42.405
The villagers clapped harder, and the women screamed louder.

11
00:00:42.406 --> 00:00:47.622
"Oh, Twi, I’m scared!" cried Mandy.

12
00:00:47.623 --> 00:00:51.474
"Shh, Mandy," whispered Twi.

13
00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:55.774
"Yeah, Mandy, cool it," said Vinnie.

14
00:00:55.775 --> 00:00:59.295
Soon, everything got quiet.

15
00:00:59.296 --> 00:01:03.284
Gau sat up, and Kashe walked over to him.

16
00:01:03.285 --> 00:01:06.801
The other villagers gathered around.

17
00:01:06.802 --> 00:01:10.020
An old man was sitting close by.

18
00:01:10.021 --> 00:01:15.441
He was holding a rock and dipping his fingers into some kind of paint.

19
00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.887
He started drawing something on the rock.

20
00:01:18.888 --> 00:01:23.502
"What’s he doing?" Mandy asked Twi.

21
00:01:23.503 --> 00:01:28.604
"He is recording the healing on a rock," explained Twi.

22
00:01:28.605 --> 00:01:33.415
"His picture proves our healers have great power.

23
00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:38.024
We use these rocks to tell the story to our children."

24
00:01:38.025 --> 00:01:41.210
"Stories?" asked Vinnie.

25
00:01:41.211 --> 00:01:44.090
"Yes," said Twi.

26
00:01:44.091 --> 00:01:47.811
"Sometimes we have bigger stories to tell.

27
00:01:47.812 --> 00:01:51.006
So we put them on bigger rocks."

28
00:01:51.007 --> 00:01:54.267
"Come," Twi’s mother called.

29
00:01:54.268 --> 00:01:57.594
"We have delicious mongongo!"

30
00:01:57.595 --> 00:02:00.203
Everyone cheered.

31
00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:04.582
Twi brought over two bowls for Vinnie and Mandy.

32
00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:09.318
Mandy took a sip.

33
00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:13.327
"It’s wonderful!" she said.

34
00:02:13.328 --> 00:02:17.578
Kashe came over and sat beside Vinnie and Mandy.

35
00:02:17.579 --> 00:02:21.416
They all watched some boys playing a game.

36
00:02:21.417 --> 00:02:28.150
They were throwing long wooden sticks at a round target made out of woven grass.

37
00:02:28.151 --> 00:02:33.354
"The little ones are already practicing to be good hunters," said Kashe.

38
00:02:33.355 --> 00:02:37.168
"One day you’ll be a fine hunter too, Vinnie."

39
00:02:37.169 --> 00:02:43.371
"Vinnie," said Mandy, "I think I know what the glowing thing is."

40
00:02:43.372 --> 00:02:46.822
"What is it?" asked Vinnie.

41
00:02:46.823 --> 00:02:50.210
He didn’t want to take the photo out.

42
00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:53.305
All the villagers would see it.

43
00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:54.703
"It’s a rock.

44
00:02:54.704 --> 00:03:00.919
I saw it when I was gathering mongongo nuts with Twi," Mandy said.

45
00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:05.727
"But you didn’t return home," Vinnie pointed out.

46
00:03:05.728 --> 00:03:07.911
She thought for a moment.

47
00:03:07.912 --> 00:03:12.407
"I know. It’s strange."

48
00:03:12.408 --> 00:03:13.968
"You should get some rest,"

49
00:03:13.969 --> 00:03:17.069
said Kashe, turning to the children.

50
00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.285
"We are moving our village tomorrow."

51
00:03:20.286 --> 00:03:23.820
"Where?" asked Vinnie.

52
00:03:23.821 --> 00:03:25.837
"To a place with fresh water,"

53
00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:29.615
Kashe answered, and went inside a hut.

54
00:03:29.616 --> 00:03:37.783
"Vinnie," Mandy whispered, "We can’t go with them—we have to get home!"

55
00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:43.034
The children quietly left the village and went toward the cave.

56
00:03:43.035 --> 00:03:45.733
Nobody saw them leave.

57
00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.936
Vinnie took out the photo.

58
00:03:47.937 --> 00:03:50.212
It was glowing blue.

59
00:03:50.213 --> 00:03:53.858
"We’re close," said Mandy.

60
00:03:53.859 --> 00:03:58.632
They walked over to the painted rock just inside the cave.

61
00:03:58.633 --> 00:04:02.007
"This is it!" she said.

62
00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:05.452
She could see animals and dancing men.

63
00:04:05.453 --> 00:04:08.100
Vinnie looked at the photo.

64
00:04:08.101 --> 00:04:12.785
"But why weren’t you sent home when you were here with Twi?"

65
00:04:12.786 --> 00:04:16.791
"I don’t . . ." Mandy began.

66
00:04:16.792 --> 00:04:24.227
"Wait—maybe because we always have to go photo traveling together!" she cried.

67
00:04:24.228 --> 00:04:27.882
The photo was glowing red.

68
00:04:27.883 --> 00:04:31.198
"That’s it!" shouted Vinnie.

69
00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:38.557
The children fell down the dark tunnel.

